{"name":"Sea Kale","hex":"#30a299","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea kale","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Crambe maritima, a halophytic perennial plant that grows wild along the coasts of Europe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_kale"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crambe maritima","blocks":[{"text":"Crambe maritima, common name sea kale, seakale or crambe, is a species of halophytic (salt-tolerant) flowering plant in the genus Crambe of the family Brassicaceae. It grows wild along the coasts of mainland Europe and the British Isles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Crambe_Maritima_Estonia.jpg/330px-Crambe_Maritima_Estonia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crambe_maritima"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea"},{"title":"Kale","blocks":[{"text":"Kale, also called leaf cabbage, belongs to a group of cabbage cultivars primarily grown for their edible leaves, but it is also used as an ornamental plant. Its multiple different cultivars vary quite a bit in appearance; the leaves can be bumpy, curly, or flat, and the color ranges from purple to green."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Boerenkool.jpg/330px-Boerenkool.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kale"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Crambe_maritima_flowers_062811.jpg/500px-Crambe_maritima_flowers_062811.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Crambe_maritima_flowers_062811.jpg/1280px-Crambe_maritima_flowers_062811.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Crambe_maritima_flowers_062811.jpg/500px-Crambe_maritima_flowers_062811.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crambe maritima flowers; Saaremaa, Estonia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrambe_maritima_flowers_062811.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Shingle_beach_and_sea_kale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1442148.jpg/500px-Shingle_beach_and_sea_kale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1442148.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Shingle_beach_and_sea_kale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1442148.jpg/500px-Shingle_beach_and_sea_kale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1442148.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shingle beach with sea kale, Landguard Fort, Suffolk","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShingle_beach_and_sea_kale_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1442148.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Shoreham_Beach_SNCI_-_geograph.org.uk_-_179687.jpg/500px-Shoreham_Beach_SNCI_-_geograph.org.uk_-_179687.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Shoreham_Beach_SNCI_-_geograph.org.uk_-_179687.jpg/500px-Shoreham_Beach_SNCI_-_geograph.org.uk_-_179687.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea kale growin